{"kind":"request","text":"Builder: check job budgets and deadlines (simplification review 55563589, findings COST-04, COST-05, COST-13). (1) A rejected check job is re-owed at +30 s with no attempt limit (room/src/jobs.ts:464-466, also :160 and :415), and jobs.ts never reads the checker's retryable flag (checkers/src/checker.ts:97-99 marks oversized output as not worth retrying). A test that prints more than 8 MiB runs about 576 containers a day until the generation is superseded, predicted at $43 a month per stuck job. Honour retryable, cap attempts, back off exponentially, and raise attention when the cap is reached. (2) The runner ignores the job deadline: timeoutSeconds has no maximum (policy/src/validate.ts:194-195), each runner step gets 600 s regardless (checkers/src/runner.ts:110; sandbox.ts:184), the deadline is checked only at the start (job.ts:155-156), and the Room re-issues a new container once the deadline passes while the old one may still run (jobs.ts:156-160). Abort runner steps at the job deadline and cap timeoutSeconds. (3) There is no per-room concurrency or daily budget for jobs (jobs.ts:138-160 issues every due job; checkers/src/worker.ts:51 creates a runner per attempt; no max_instances in checkers/wrangler.spike.jsonc). Fifty open proposals times three checkers is 150 standard-1 containers at once from one room. Add a per-room concurrency limit and a daily job budget as policy or deployment settings, and set max_instances.","body":{"conditions":"Tests: a non-retryable failure is not retried; attempts cap with attention; a step is aborted at the deadline; concurrency and budget limits refuse or defer jobs; wrangler configs set max_instances; root gates pass; checker review.","target_head":"a6330262b1a609843308d9a493dbd6132d428499","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}